 "hair_length": {
  "how_to_use": "tools/hair_length.py: visible length = stretched length x (1 - shrinkage). after/before = (1 - after_shrinkage of the rule) / (1 - shrinkage of the avatar's curl pattern). Lengths in head heights from the top of the head; the prompt names the nearest body landmark. after_shrinkage null = the style keeps the curl pattern, so the length stays. Coily blowouts keep part of their texture (SS_t4_roundbrush 0.4): a shoulder-length 4B afro ends at the middle of the chest, not lower; the amount of hair never grows.",
  "source": "common curl-shrinkage ranges (type 2 ~5-15%, 3A-3C ~30-50%, 4A-4C ~50-75%); we use the low end because a heat style rarely releases all of it. Checked against Gustavo's before/after avatars (2026-10-23): auto curler on straight hair x0.83, sleek blowout on 3C x1.42 in his images; the model gives x0.80 and x1.53.",
